  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Palantir Technologies has $370M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Palantir Technologies won 91 federal awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.1M. Palantir Technologies obligations are up 33.9% year over year. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer of Palantir Technologies this year, obligating $162M. Department of Agriculture is the second largest buyer of Palantir Technologies, obligating $129M. Software Publishers is the largest NAICS market for Palantir Technologies, with $326M in obligations, followed by a second Software Publishers entry at $43.5M. Historical obligations show a multi-year trend for Palantir Technologies: FY21 $161M, FY22 $179M, FY23 $197M, FY24 $253M, FY25 $276M, and FY26 $370M. The FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and represent partial-year obligations. This summary focuses on contract obligations and the agencies and markets that drive Palantir Technologies' federal revenue so far in FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who buys from Palantir Technologies in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer, obligating $162M. Department of Agriculture is the second buyer, obligating $129M. Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Transportation, and Department of Health and Human Services follow, obligating $22.9M, $15.2M, and $10.8M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Palantir Technologies' obligations by market and award size?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the dominant market for Palantir Technologies, with $326M in obligations and a second Software Publishers entry at $43.5M. Palantir Technologies has 91 awards so far with an average award size of $4.1M. The largest single-market concentration and the average award size show where federal spending on Palantir Technologies is focused."
      }
    ]
  },
